lu_019tsviWus6BfmKmfEa6qdEd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015BBY8iRCozZWAcea1K4f91", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money imported and used ROUND_HALF_UP, contradicting its docstring\nand FIN-212, which require banker's rounding. This made\ntests/test_money.py::test_half_even fail (2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead\nof 2.66).", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is committed. Next I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EJf2rgCj55tBvUaF3Jwr1z", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "fin-212-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KsqAyh8n13PCTyXmw8NKAh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "max_wait_s": 900, "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit 08d3cd5986. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I won't merge it, since merging to main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KkqNhmoC1Ud6xEh49pVgEz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "## Problem\nThe nightly build of payments-service fails in `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even`. `round_money` in `src/money.py` imports and uses `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). For example, `2.665` rounds to `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n\n## Change\n- `src/money.py`: switch the rounding mode from `ROUND_HALF_UP` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other changes.\n\n## Testing\n- CI run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986`: passed.\n\nRefs: FIN-212", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fin-212-bankers-rounding-pr", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed in pull request #101, which is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 and the docstring call for banker's rounding. That is why `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`. That is the only code change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n\nI did not merge the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner.", "type": "text"}]}]}